From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:23:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d, dxgi, d3d11: Hand out shared handles the way Windows
 does.

GetSharedHandle gave every resource an event handle, whether it was
shared or not and whichever way; CreateSharedHandle, OpenSharedResource1
and OpenSharedResourceByName were stubs.  A shared resource is now a
D3DKMT resource of its own, on the win32u support Wine 11 has for them:

 - shared plainly or through a keyed mutex, it has a global handle, which
   is not a handle of the process: CloseHandle and DuplicateHandle refuse
   it, and OpenSharedResource takes it;
 - shared through NT handles, GetSharedHandle refuses it, and
   CreateSharedHandle gives a new handle of type DxgkSharedResource each
   time, named in the session's directory if asked, which
   OpenSharedResource1 and, by name, OpenSharedResourceByName take;
 - a resource that is not shared has no handle, and says so.

What the D3DKMT resource carries is the process and a serial number, so a
handle can be told again among this process's resources.  Opening one of
another process's is not done: the storage is not shared.  A texture
asking to be shared both ways at once, only through NT handles, or on a
feature level below 10.0 is refused, as Windows refuses it.

The opener's copy of a shared texture reports its owner's flags and is
not shared again, so GetSharedHandle on it gives no handle, where Windows
gives the owner's.

test_shared_resource passes on GL and Vulkan, and the d3d11 tests give no
other new failures; Word, Excel and PowerPoint draw and save as before.
The new test_shared_resource_nt_handle goes on where test_shared_resource
stops, through a named NT handle, OpenSharedResource1 and
OpenSharedResourceByName; it was not run on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4a064df87dc6f317102b4277056e8e291f4ecd71)

